    description: "Third occurrence of one shape: INV-bofab (09-03), INV-fugus (09-23, datetime.date.today), now datetime.date.fromisoformat. Each time one module the catalogue could not classify withheld every self-claim verdict (confirmed_with_caveats -> inconclusive, opaque_boundary dropped), seen only by the cron self-claims-gate. Reproduced 2026-10-14 at ffe97d229f in a pinned worktree (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/claims_10142026): drift line-for-line the cron's; with datetime.date declared complete the same run reports 'OK -- 18 claims unchanged (18 confirmed_with_caveats)'. Instance fix on branch jgstern-agent/fix/self-claims-datetime-date. STRUCTURAL gap open: no per-PR check catches the next one. Candidate: a fast AST check over packages/*/src that every dotted stdlib call's module is row-covered or module_completeness-declared, run per PR."  # 897b
    fields:  # 897b
      statement: "A shipped-code call into a stdlib member the python I/O catalogue neither rows nor enumerates cannot reach dev without a per-PR failure; today it reaches dev and only the cron self-claims-gate sees it."  # 897b
      root_cause: "io_primitives/python.yaml declared datetime.datetime complete but not datetime.date, so the tracker priority_trend.py / cli.py call datetime.date.fromisoformat made datetime.date an unclassifiable module, which withholds every clean verdict. The detection gap: the self-claims gate needs a ~6 min self-map and runs only on the cron."  # 897b
